<%#
  Where Stripe sends a visitor back after its checkout (CartController#
  thanks), in the site's frame as the cart is (CartHelper draws it): a band
  of deep water saying, in plain words, whether the order is paid, not
  yet, or expired, or that whether it is paid could not be asked just now
  (asked: false); then the order's lines as they were sold, its total, and
  the way back: to the shop once it is paid, otherwise to the cart, which
  still holds what was not paid for.
  order: the order the session is of.
-%>
<%- title, said = order_words(order, asked) -%>
<%- back = order.status == "paid" ? [ shop_path, "Back to the shop" ] : [ "/cart", "Back to your cart" ] -%>
<%= cart_head(title, said) %><%= order_body(order.lines, order.total, order.currency, *back) -%>
